      "content": "thanks for these. i noticed a pretty big difference in the types of backgrounds you picked for the two products. for the luxury skincare, you went with someone from a wealthy area like Beverly Hills, but for the cleaners, you went with a taxi driver from Mexico City. \n\ncan you explain the logic behind why those specific cultural backgrounds and occupations are better suited for these products? like, why wouldn't a person from a more \"traditional\" or immigrant background be the target for the luxury line, or why wouldn't a high-earning professional be the one looking for budget cleaners?",
